{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## P1 deep dive (overlap / similar-ticket surfacing) — research record\n\n### Three investigations\n1. Implementation (src/rebar/llm/overlap, enrich.py, enrich_drain.py, hooks): overlap never ran at CREATE; only after plan-review certification. Digests (LLM-extracted Cupid digest, ~2.8 KB signed event) AND queue coordination (ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH) persisted as events on the shared auto-pushed tickets branch. No persisted index: each query re-reduces every ticket (~48 s on this store, measured). 105,197 of 147,074 event files (71.5%) are overlap sidecars; 93% of digests recomputed for unchanged content (unconditional enqueue on every cert; freshness key includes the environment-local model string, causing cross-environment ping-pong). Drain gate rides every store write and spawns a detached interpreter. Reusable and sound: ticket_digest schema + prompt, BM25F scorer (retrieve.py ~65 LOC pure fn), graph exclusion, judge prompt + batch contract + both-orderings aggregation, calibration script/data, content-hash freshness idea, recent_creates.py journal as the model for per-clone derived state. Verdict: right retrieval pattern; the structural flaw is ADR 0086 §3 \"the event store IS the enrichment queue\".\n2. Ticket history: epic only-crave-art (bd83-c56f-1f72-4ef2), 7 children landed 07-09/10, ADR 0086. Rationale recorded: embeddings rejected on experiment (digest-BM25F recall@20 = 1.0 on 8 paraphrase pairs); events-on-branch chosen because \"a separate SQLite file could not live on a shared path\"; detached drain chosen for zero client setup (git gc --auto analogy); success metric was an offline fixture only. Bug clusters: (A) prune outside the lock (3a33, 3435, 4f8d, ac26, 4c1c, 88eb); (B) prune breaks union-merge (8185, 55bc) which removed the only growth bound; (C) unbounded growth / write storm (8bef, a453, 62ab, 4eae, ADR 0106); (D) gate on every write is O(store) (9c90, 958e, 4144, f400, 6148, a2fc), all caused_by c1de; (E) judge unbounded/miscontracted (afeb, 2391, 22da, 3939, d147); (F) detached-child hygiene (aadc, 3198, da68). \"0 findings in 2,093 reviews\" (d147) was a contract bug (confidence defaulted 0.0), fixed 08-12, never re-measured before the 08-31 disable. Create-time was never wired (eac3): 44 of 51 real duplicate pairs are semantic not lexical; same-title journal added 08-22, gated on the same key, so the 08-31 flip also disabled it. Disable tickets 62ab (08-27, drain off) and 4eae (08-31, producer off) framed as reversible; scratch stability plan framed as retire-next-program. Recorded remediation ideas: 4520, 475e, 9c90 option B (persistent HEAD-keyed derived index), 393a/dd37 (batch-only enrichment tiers), eac3 (persistent title index), ADR 0106.\n3. OSS survey (git-bug, Fossil, jj, Cargo, Zoekt, Gitea, Zulip, Discourse, Bugzilla, GitLab, GitHub, Linear, Sentry, mdBook, Omnisearch): every comparable system keeps the index as a disposable, version-keyed local cache outside the replicated store (e.g. .git/git-bug/{cache,indexes}), rebuilt or caught up incrementally in the reader's process; compose-time similarity is lexical-first, capped 3-5, non-blocking; ML/LLM gated and off the write path. No surveyed project persists derived search data as records in the primary store or spawns per-write background indexers coordinated by leases.\n\n### Synthesis\nSearch pattern (lexical retrieve, advisory LLM judge, never auto-link) = sound and matches practice. Persistence/coordination architecture (branch as cache + queue, write-path spawn, leases) = pattern no comparable project uses and the root of all six bug clusters. Recommended next-iteration shape: per-clone SQLite (FTS5 + optional trigram) under .git/rebar or XDG cache keyed by tickets HEAD SHA + format version; incremental catch-up in the reader's process; no write-path spawn; single-writer BEGIN IMMEDIATE, skip on contention; create-time query on title + 200 chars of body, top 3-5, advisory; digests/embeddings optional in the catch-up step; LLM judge on demand over ≤10 candidates; MCP server may pre-warm on a timer but correctness never depends on it. Open design question: raw-text FTS vs LLM-digest recall on the 51 known duplicate pairs (digest normalization is what gave paraphrase recall).\n\nRecommendation to operator: P1-A (design-record epic + removal referencing the removal commit; keep the four event-type names for parsing; decouple and re-enable the create-time title journal; tombstone the 13 config keys).\n\n## Premise re-check of B/C after operator rulings\nItems whose evidence was about this deployment rather than the product: P15 (5.5 events/ticket is this store; compaction is a documented user feature; post-close trigger serves clients without CI), P18 (5 cache entries is this host; pinned ticket view underpins attested-gate reproducibility), P19 (mapping overlay is the documented client-vocabulary surface; ADR 0097 many-to-many is \"the common case\"; canary filing is a documented contract), P17 (re-review rate is this deployment; verdict enum is a public outputSchema), P11 partially (60-day reference heuristic), P16 partially (tombstones and alias windows are client promises per docs/api-stability.md), P14 partially (completion-recovery collapse based on this deployment's failure rates), P9 remainder (client-authored workflows and client routing select the \"unused\" features). Structural items unaffected: P12, P13(a), P14(a,b), P20, P21."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788734580883965869,"uuid":"e1a42ee0-6909-4b90-b5d5-ba70c0cdf938"}